  <hr class="rule-accent" />

  <p>
    I'm Christopher — an economist working on macroeconomic forecasting, labour markets, and
    policy evaluation. At <a href="https://www.alleghenyecon.com">Allegheny Economic Research</a>
    I build forecasts, analyse labour and employment data, and evaluate policy interventions with
    difference-in-differences and synthetic control methods, then write it up for government and
    private-sector clients. I work in Stata, R, Python, and SQL.
  </p>

  <p>
    Southeast Asia is where I want to apply that work. I lived and worked in Hà Nội from 2016 to
    2020, speak, read, and write Vietnamese at an advanced level, and have working Bahasa
    Indonesia and elementary Thai. My graduate training pairs an MSc in Development Economics
    (<a href="http://www.city.ac.uk">City, University of London</a>, Distinction), with a
    dissertation on female labour force participation across Southeast Asian countries, and an
    MA in Southeast Asian Studies (<a href="https://www.soas.ac.uk/">SOAS, University of
    London</a>, Distinction) covering the political economies of Vietnam, Thailand, and
    Indonesia.
  </p>

