  <h2>What I Work On</h2>

  <ul class="languages">
    <li><strong>Macroeconomic forecasting</strong> — building and maintaining forecasts and the data behind them.</li>
    <li><strong>Labour markets</strong> — employment data, labour-market dynamics, and female labour force participation.</li>
    <li><strong>Policy evaluation</strong> — difference-in-differences and synthetic control, written up for non-specialist readers.</li>
    <li><strong>Data and reporting</strong> — reproducible pipelines, databases, and dashboards, from ten years on the data side of the private sector.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Southeast Asia</h2>

  <p>
    <strong>Viet Nam</strong> is my deepest country knowledge: four years running a consultancy
    in Hà Nội, a dissertation on the Vietnamese state's COVID-19 response, and an ongoing
    project on how US tariffs affect Viet Nam's export economy.
    <strong>Indonesia</strong>: two terms of Bahasa Indonesia study and a policy brief on the
    Nusantara capital relocation. <strong>Thailand</strong>: graduate coursework and a country
    brief on Thai political developments. Across the region, my MSc work compares female labour
    force participation in ASEAN economies.
  </p>

