  <h2>Background</h2>

  <p>
    Before economics I spent about a decade on the data and software side of the private sector,
    starting at <a href="https://www.novachem.com">NOVA Chemicals</a>, where I designed SQL
    databases and reporting for the financial analytics team. I then ran two small businesses in
    Pittsburgh, and from 2016 to 2020 co-founded and ran Southern Cross Technologies, a technology
    and data consultancy in Hà Nội with clients across Vietnam, Indonesia, and Thailand. Running it
    day to day taught me how Vietnam's regulatory environment, licensing, and business conditions
    work in practice. I returned to graduate school from 2021 to 2024 and joined Allegheny Economic
    Research in 2023.
  </p>

  <p>
    Founder, <a href="https://mekong-advisory-main.vercel.app">Mekong Advisory</a> — an independent
    economic consultancy focused on the Greater Mekong Subregion (Vietnam, Thailand, Cambodia,
    Laos, Myanmar), producing evidence-based analysis for policymakers, institutions, and
    investors.
  </p>

  <h2>For Editors</h2>

  <p>
    I pitch analysis and explainer pieces on Southeast Asian economies — labour markets, trade
    and investment exposure, state capacity, and development economics. Recent work includes an
    analysis of Viet Nam's exposure to US tariff policy, an MA dissertation on how Vietnam's
    party-state governance shaped its COVID-19 response, and a policy brief on Indonesia's capital
    relocation (<a href="/research">see Research</a> for details). Reach me at
    <a href="mailto:chrisjoy@fastmail.com">chrisjoy@fastmail.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Currently</h2>

  <p>
    Writing a project on Viet Nam and US tariffs. Reading <em>Seeing Like a State</em> by
    James C. Scott.
  </p>
